<title>USA: Table of U.S. industrial production revisions.</title>
<headline>Table of U.S. industrial production revisions.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve Board Monday issued revised historical data from its monthly report on industrial production and factory capacity use back to 1977.</p>
<p>In the following, &quot;Output&quot; is industrial production percent change in month or year, and &quot;Cap Use&quot; is percent of factory capacity use in a month or year. Monthly data is seasonally adjusted, annual data is not.  </p>
<p> -     NEW METHOD	 OLD METHOD</p>
<p> 1996: Output/Cap Use   Output/Cap Use</p>
<p> Dec     0.7   83.5	 0.8   83.8</p>
<p> Nov     0.8   83.2	 0.8   83.4</p>
<p> Oct    Unch   82.8	-0.1   83.0</p>
<p> Sept    0.1   83.1	 0.2   83.4</p>
<p> Aug     0.3   83.2	 0.5   83.5</p>
<p> July   Unch   83.2	Unch   83.4</p>
<p> June    0.6   83.5	 0.8   83.7</p>
<p> May     0.4   83.2	 0.7   83.3</p>
<p> Apr     0.9   83.1	 0.8   83.0</p>
<p> Mar    -0.5   82.6	-0.5   82.6</p>
<p> Feb     1.3   83.2	 1.3   83.3</p>
<p> Jan    -0.4   82.4	-0.2   82.4</p>
<p> -     NEW METHOD	 OLD METHOD</p>
<p> Year: Output/Cap Use   Output/Cap Use</p>
<p> 1996    2.7   83.1	 3.2   83.2</p>
<p> 1995    3.3   83.8	 3.2   83.8</p>
<p> 1994    5.0   83.7	 5.9   83.9</p>
<p> 1993    3.4   81.6	 3.5   81.4</p>
<p> 1992    3.2   80.4	 3.4   80.3</p>
<p> 1991   -2.0   79.2	-1.8   79.2</p>
<p> 1990   -0.2   82.3	Unch   82.1</p>
<p> 1989    1.8   84.0	 1.5   83.7</p>
<p> 1988    4.4   83.9	 4.4   83.7</p>
<p> 1987    4.6   81.3	 4.9   81.5</p>
<p>The Fed provided annual revised industrial production and capacity use rates under new method only through 1987, though it reformulated indexes and utilization rates back to 1977.</p>
</text>
